From: Bo-Cun Chen <bc-bocun.chen@mediatek.com>
Date: Mon, 30 Jun 2025 11:48:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] net: export br_fdb_find_rcu for bridge flow discovery

Export br_fdb_find_rcu() so netfilter flow offload can check whether a
destination MAC is known in the bridge FDB.

The upstream dev_fill_forward_path() now accepts a caller-owned context.
Use that interface directly; the older __dev_fill_forward_path() helper
and legacy wrapper are no longer needed for bridge/VLAN discovery.

Origin: backport, https://git01.mediatek.com/plugins/gitiles/openwrt/feeds/mtk-openwrt-feeds/+/2812cb84/21.02/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-5.4/999-1718-v6.6-net-netfilter-add-nft-hw-offload.patch
Link: https://github.com/rchen14b/openwrt_rchen14b/commit/c7abf1928e3af8628697a4abb767193fb2f33366
Signed-off-by: Bo-Cun Chen <bc-bocun.chen@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
@@ -266,6 +266,7 @@ struct net_bridge_fdb_entry *br_fdb_find
 {
 	return fdb_find_rcu(&br->fdb_hash_tbl, addr, vid);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(br_fdb_find_rcu);
 
 /* When a static FDB entry is added, the mac address from the entry is
  * added to the bridge private HW address list and all required ports
